# Paths HydraCore owns outright: an SBE upgrade must never change them.
#
# These are the fork's own layers, deliberately divergent from upstream and not meant to
# track it. `upgrade_sbe.sh` restores each path to the fork's pre-merge state after an
# upstream merge and drops any file upstream added underneath it, so a merge can neither
# rewrite nor extend an owned layer. A conflict inside an owned path is therefore never
# raised for review — the fork's version always wins.
#
# One path prefix per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. A trailing slash marks
# a directory subtree; a bare path matches that file.
#
# Keep this list to genuine forked layers. A shared file that merely carries a HydraCore tweak
# (box.go, log/format.go, option/tls.go) must NOT go here: it still needs a real merge so
# upstream fixes to it are not silently dropped.

# vk_parasite and the whole call transport: pion-based, diverged from upstream's
# headless-client rewrite. Owned outright.
transport/call/

# HydraCore's own documentation set. The fork deleted upstream's sing-box docs; docs/ now
# holds only HydraCore docs (architecture, configuration, ecosystem, build-and-release).
# An SBE merge must neither resurrect upstream's docs here nor touch ours.
docs/
